 "description": "Perp price levels for one coin, from what printed rather than from a chart: executed volume at price on every venue that lists it (Binance, Bybit, BingX, Hyperliquid), with the value area (70% of volume around the POC), high-volume nodes and thin zones (prices crossed without trading, where moves tend to run); open-interest changes at price split into long and short entries; realized liquidations at price (OKX/Gate sample); and resting walls from deep books on several venues, counted only when a second snapshot 2 s later still shows them. Every level is graded by evidence \u2014 traded (volume, liquidations) > inferred (OI side) > resting (orders, which can be pulled) \u2014 and lists the other evidence at the same price (confluence). Walls larger than their venue's own daily volume are flagged. Use it for where price may stall, accelerate or meet forced flow; it is not a forecast.",
 "inputSchema": {
  "properties": {
   "hours": {
    "description": "Window in hours, 24\u2013168. Default 72.",
    "type": "integer"
   },
   "symbol": {
    "description": "Coin symbol, e.g. \"WAVES\".",
    "type": "string"
   }
  },
  "required": [
   "symbol"
  ],
  "type": "object"
 },
 "name": "flow_levels",
